('replace_p', 330, 5, "The variety of qubits is the sign of an early technology. Superconducting circuits, trapped ions, neutral atoms, photons and spins in solids are all in use, each stronger in speed, connectivity or stability, and none has won. Mature technologies usually settle on one or two platforms. Until quantum computing does, parallel investment makes sense, and no single company’s roadmap should be mistaken for the field’s. Roadmaps are plans; the platforms are the evidence."),
